//# Refer directly to the online document mentioned above for further
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:32
//# information.  Please report any errors to info@sandroid.org.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:33
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:34
//# Page 1452
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:35
//# DISPLAYS CAN BE CLASSIFIED INTO THE FOLLOWING CATEGORIES-
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:36
//#	1.  PRIORITY DISPLAYS- DISPLAYS WHICH TAKE PRIORITY OVER ALL OTHER DISPLAYS. USUALLY THESE DISPLAYS ARE SENT
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:37
//#	    OUT UNDER CRITICAL ALARM CONDITIONS.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:38
//#	2.  EXTENDED VERB DISPLAYS- ALL EXTENDED VERBS AND MARK ROUTINES SHOULD USE EXTENDED VERB (MARK) DISPLAYS.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:39
//#	3.  NORMAL DISPLAYS- ALL MISSION PROGRAM DISPLAYS WHICH INTERFACE WITH THE ASTRONAUT DURING THE NORMAL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:40
//#	    SEQUENCE OF EVENTS.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:41
//#	4.  MISC. DISPLAYS- ALL DISPLAYS NOT HANDLED BY THE DISPLAY INTERFACEROUTINES. THESE INCLUDE SUCH DISPLAYS AS
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:42
//#	    MM DISPLAYS AND SPECIAL PURPOSE DISPLAYS HANDLED BY PINBALL.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:43
//#	5.  ASTRONAUT INITIATED DISPLAYS- ALL DISPLAYS INITIATED EXTERNALLY.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:44
//#
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:45
//# THE FOLLOWING TERMS ARE USED TO DESCRIBE THE STATUS OF DISPLAYS-
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:46
//#	1.  ACTIVE-THE DISPLAY WHICH IS (1) BEING DISPLAYED TO THE ASTRONAUT AND WAITING FOR A RESPONSE OR
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:47
//#	    (2) WAITING FIRST IN LINE FOR THE ASTRONAUT TO FINISH USING THE DSKY OR (3) BEING DISPLAYED ON THE DSKY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:48
//#	    BUT NOT WAITING FOR A RESPONSE.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:49
//#	2.  INACTIVE -A DISPLAY WHICH HAS (1) BEEN ACTIVE BUT WAS INTERRUPTED BY A DISPLAY OF HIGHER PRIORITY,
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:50
//#	    (2) BEEN PUT INTO THE WAITING LIST AT TIME IT WAS REQUESTED DUE TO THE FACT A HIGHER PRIORITY DISPLAY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:51
//#	    WAS ALREADY GOING, (3) BEEN INTERRUPTED BY THE ASTRONAUT (CALLED A PINBRANCH CONDITION, SINCE THIS TYPE
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:52
//#	    OF INACTIVE DISPLAY IS USUALLY REACTIVATED ONLY BY PINBALL) OR (4) A DISPLAY WHICH HAS FINISHED BUT STILL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:53
//#	    HAS INFO SAVED FOR RESTART PURPOSES.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:54
//#
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:55
//# DISPLAY PRIORITIES WORK AS FOLLOWS-
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:56
//#	INTERRUPTS-
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:57
//#		1.  THE ASTRONAUT CAN INTERRUPT ANY DISPLAY WITH AN EXTERNAL DISPLAY REQUEST.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:58
//#		2.  INTERNAL DISPLAYS CAN NOT BE SENT OUT WHEN THE ASTRONAUT IS USING THE DSKY.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:59
//#		3.  PRIORITY DISPLAYS INTERRUPT ALL OTHER TYPES OF INTERNAL DISPLAYS.  A PRIORITY DISPLAY INTERRUPTING ANOTHER
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:60
//#		    PRIORITY DISPLAY WILL CAUSE AN ABORT UNLESS BIT14 IS SET FOR THE LINUS ROUTINE.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:61
//#		4.  A MARK DISPLAY INTERRUPTS ANY NORMAL DISPLAY.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:62
//#		5.  A MARK THAT INTERRUPTS A MARK COMPLETELY REPLACES IT.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:63
//#
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:64
//# 	ORDER OF WAITING DISPLAYS-
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:65
//#		1.  ASTRONAUT EXTERNAL USE
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:66
//#		2.  PRIORITY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:67
//#		3.  INTERRUPTED MARK
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:68
//#		4.  INTERRUPTED NORMAL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:69
//#		5.  MARK TO BE REQUESTED (SEE DESCRIPTION OF ENDMARK)
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:70
//#		6.  MARK WAITING
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:71
//#		7.  NORMAL WAITING
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:72
//#
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:73
//# Page 1453
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:74
//# THE DISPLAY ROUTINES ARE INTENDED TO SERVE AS AN INTERFACE BETWEEN THE USER AND PINBALL.  THE
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:75
//# FOLLOWING STATEMENTS CAN BE MADE ABOUT NORMAL DISPLAYS AND PRIORITY DISPLAYS (A DESCRIPTION OF MARK ROUTINES
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:76
//# WILL FOLLOW LATER):
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:77
//#	1.  ALL ROUTINES THAT END IN R HAVE AN IMMEDIATE RETURN TO THE USER.  FOR ALL FLASHING DISPLAYS THIS RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:78
//#	    IS TO THE USERS CALL CADR +4.  FOR THE ONLY NON FLASHING IMMEDIATE RETURN DISPLAY (GODSPR) THIS RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:79
//#	    IS TO THE USERS CALLING LOC +1.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:80
//#	2.  ALL ROUTINES NOT ENDING IN R DO NOT DO AN IMMEDIATE RETURN TO THE USER.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:81
//#	3.  ALL ROUTINES THAT END IN R START A SEPARATE JOB (MAKEPLAY) WITH USERS JOB PRIORITY.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:82
//#	4.  ALL ROUTINES NOT ENDING IN R BRANCH DIRECTLY TO MAKEPLAY WHICH MAKES THESE DISPLAYS A PART OF THE
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:83
//#	    USERS JOB.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:84
//#	5.  ALL DISPLAY ROUTINES ARE CALLED VIA BANKCALL.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:85
//#	6.  TO RESTART A DISPLAY THE USER WILL GENERALLY USE A PHASE OF ONE WITH DESIRED RESTART GROUP (SEE
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:86
//#	    DESCRIPTION OF RESTARTS).
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:87
//#	7.  ALL FLASHING DISPLAYS HAVE 3 RETURNS TO THE USER FROM ASTRONAUT RESPONSES.  A TERMINATE (V34) BRANCHES
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:88
//#	    TO THE USERS CALL CADR +1.  A PROCEED (V33) BRANCHES TO THE USERS CALL CADR +2.  AN ENTER OR RECYCLE
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:89
//#	    (V32) BRANCHES TO THE USERS CALL CADR +3.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:90
//#	8.  ALL ROUTINES MUST BE USED UNDER EXECUTIVE CONTROL.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:91
//#
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:92
//# A DESCRIPTION OF EACH ROUTINE WITH AN EXAMPLE FOLLOWS:
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:93
//#	GODSP IS USED TO DISPLAY A VERB NOUN ARRIVING IN A.  NO RETURN IS MADE TO THE USER.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:94
//#		1.  GODSP IS NOT RESTARTABLE
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:95
//#		2.  A VERB PASTE WITH GODSP ALWAYS TURNS ON THE FLASH.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:96
//#				CAF	VXXNYY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:97
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:98
//#				CADR	GODSP
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:99
//#			VXXNYY	OCT	OXXYY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:100
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:101
//#	GODSPR IS THE SAME AS GODSP ONLY RETURN IS TO THE USER.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:102
//#				CAF	VXXNYY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:103
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:104
//#				CADR	GODSPR
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:105
//#				...	...		# IMMEDIATE RETURN OF GODSPR
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:106
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:107
//#	GOFLASH DISPLAYS A FLASHING VERB NOUN WITH NO IMMEDIATE RETURN TO THE USER. 3 RETURNS ARE POSSIBLE FORM
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:108
//#	THE ASTRONAUT (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:109
//#				CAF	VXXNYY		# VXX NYY WILL BE A FLASHING VERB NOUN.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:110
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:111
//#				CADR	GOFLASH
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:112
//#				...	...		# TERMINATE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:113
//#				...	...		# PROCEED RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:114
//#				...	...		# ENTER OR RECYCLE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:115
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:116
//#	GOPERF1 IS ENTERED WITH DESIRED CHECKLIST VALUE IN A.  GOPERF1 WILL DISPLAY THIS VALUE IN R1 BY MEANS OF A
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:117
//# Page 1454
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:118
//# 	V01 N25.A FLASHING PLEASE PERFORM ON CHECKLIST (V50 N25) IS THEN DISPLAYED.  NO IMMEDIATE RETURN IS MADE TO
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:119
//# 	USER (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:120
//#	GOPERF1 BLANKS REGISTERS R2 AND R3
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:121
//#				CAF	OCTXX		# CODE FOR CHECKLIST VALUE XX
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:122
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:123
//#				CADR	GOPERF1
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:124
//#				...	...		# TERMINATE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:125
//#				...	...		# PROCEED RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:126
//#				...	...		# ENTER RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:127
//#	GOPERF2 IS ENTERED WITH A VARIABLE NOUN AND V01 (V00 FOR N10 OR N11) IN A.  GOPERF2 WILL FIRST DISPLAY THE
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:128
//# 	REQUESTED NOUN BY MEANS OF A V01NYY OR A V00NYY. PLEASE PERFORM ON NOUN (V50 NYY) THEN BECOMES A FLASHING
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:129
//#	DISPLAY.  NO IMMEDIATE RETURN IS MADE TO THE USER (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:130
//#	GOPERF2 DOES NOT BLANK ANY REGISTERS
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:131
//#				CAF	VXXNYY		# VARIABLE NOUN YY. XX=00 OR 01.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:132
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:133
//#				CADR	GOPERF2
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:134
//#				...	...		# TERMINATE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:135
//#				...	...		# PROCEED RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:136
//#				...	...		# ENTER RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:137
//#	GOPERF3 IS USED FOR A PLEASE PERFORM ON A PROGRAM NUMBER.  THE DESIRED PROGRAM NO. IS ENTERED IN A.  GOPERF3
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:138
//#	DISPLAYS THE NO. BY MEANS OF A V06 N07 FOLLOWED BY A FLASHING V50 N07 FOR A PLEASE PERFORM. NO IMMEDIATE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:139
//#	IS MADE TO THE USER (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:140
//#	GOPERF3 BLANKS REGISTERS R2 AND R3
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:141
//#				CAF	DECXX		# REQUEST PERFORM ON PXX
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:142
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:143
//#				CADR	GOPERF3
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:144
//#				...	...		# TERMINATE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:145
//#				...	...		# PROCEED RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:146
//#				...	...		# ENTER RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:147
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:148
//#	GOPERF4 IS USED FOR A PLEASE PERFORM ON AN OPTION. THE DESIRED OPTION IS ENTERED IN A AND STORED IN OPTION1.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:149
//#	GOPERF4 DISPLAYS R1 AND R2 BY MEANS OF A V04N06 FOLLOWED BY A FLASHING V50N06 FOR A PLEASE PERFORM.  NO
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:150
//#	IMMEDIATE RETURN IS MADE TO THE USER (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:151
//#				CAF	OCTXX		# REQUEST PERFORM ON OPTION XX
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:152
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:153
//#				CADR	GOPERF4
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:154
//#				...	...		# TERMINATE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:155
//#				...	...		# PROCEED RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:156
//#				...	...		# ENTER RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:157
//#	GOPERF4 BLANKS REGISTER R3
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:158
//#
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:159
//# Page 1455
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:160
//#	GODSPRET IS USED TO DISPLAY A VERB NOUN ARRIVING IN A WITH A RETURN TO THE USER AFTER THE DISPLAY HAS BEEN SENT
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:161
//#	OUT.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:162
//#				CAF	VXXXNYY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:163
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:164
//#				CADR	GODSPRET
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:165
//#				...	...		# RETURN TO USER
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:166
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:167
//#	REGODSP IS USED TO DISPLAY A VERB NOUN ARRIVING IN A.  REGODSP IS THE SAME AS GODSP ONLY REGODSP REPLACES ANY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:168
//# 	ACTIVE NORMAL DISPLAY IF ONE WAS ACTIVE.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:169
//#				CAF	VXXNYY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:170
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:171
//#				CADR	REGODSP
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:172
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:173
//#	REFLASH IS THE SAME AS GOFLASH ONLY REFLASH REPLACES ANY ACTIVE NORMAL DISPLAY IF ONE WAS ACTIVE.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:174
//#				CAF	VXXNYY		# VXX NYY WILL BE A FLASHING VERB NOUN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:175
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:176
//#				CADR	REFLASH
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:177
//#				...	...		# TERMINATE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:178
//#				...	...		# PROCEED RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:179
//#				...	...		# ENTER RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:180
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:181
//# 	GOFLASHR IF SAME AS GOFLASH ONLY AN IMMEDIATE RETURN IS MADE TO THE USERS CALL CADR +4.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:182
//#				CAF	VXXNYY
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:183
//#				TC	BANKCALL
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:184
//#				CADR	GOFLASHR
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:185
//#				...	...		# TERMINATE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:186
//#				...	...		# PROCEED RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:187
//#				...	...		# ENTER OR RECYCLE RETURN
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:188
//#				...	...		# IMMEDIATE RETURN FROM GOFLASHR
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:189
//
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:190
//#	GOPERF1R IS THE SAME AS GOPERF1 ONLY GOPERF1R HAS AN IMMEDIATE RETURN TO USERS CALL CADR +4.
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:191
//#	GOPERF1R BLANKS REGISTERS R2 AND R3
// PORT: SOURCE DISPLAY_INTERFACE_ROUTINES.agc:192
